📜 .cursorrules (Modular PHP CMS Project Rules)

📁 Directory Structure

The base structure must follow this layout:

/app        → Controllers, Models, Views  
/core       → Core system, classes, middleware  
/config     → Configurations, routes, database settings  
/content    → Custom themes and modules  
    ├── /themes     → Each theme in its own folder, using Tailwind CSS  
    └── /modules    → Each module in its own folder  
/admin      → Admin panel files (Tailwind-based, separate from modules)  
/public     → Public assets: CSS, JS, images, uploads

No other root-level folders should be created unless explicitly stated.

🧩 Modules (content/modules)

- All modules are placed inside content/modules/<ModuleName>/.
- Each module may include controllers/, models/, views/ directories.
- Modules must be auto-discoverable by the core system.
- Existing modules must not break due to additions.
- Routes can be defined inside the module or registered in config/routes.php.
- All changes must be logged in a process.md file (name, purpose, date, etc.).

🎨 Themes (content/themes)

- Themes go inside content/themes/<ThemeName>/.
- Must use Tailwind CSS for styling.
- Theme system should dynamically load templates from here.
- Active theme config is defined in config/config.php or similar.
- Theme folder may include views/, partials/, layouts/, and assets/.

⚙️ MVC System

- New controllers go in app/controllers/ or module's controllers/.
- Views should be either in app/views/ or in themes.
- Controller path: /module/controller/action/param
- Route collisions should gracefully fallback.

🔐 Security Rules

- Use htmlspecialchars, strip_tags for XSS protection.
- Every form must include and validate CSRF tokens.
- Use PDO + prepared statements for DB operations.
- Passwords: use password_hash and password_verify.
- Middleware should cover:  
  - Auth  
  - CSRF  
  - Input sanitization  
  - Role-based access control

✅ Form Validation

- A centralized validator (e.g., app/Validation/Validator.php) should be created.
- Built-in rules: required, email, min/maxLength, numeric, etc.
- Input should be validated before and after submission.
- Validation errors must be shown clearly to users.

🌐 Multilingual Support

- URL-based structure: /en/, /tr/, etc.
- Translation files inside config/lang/en.php, tr.php, etc.
- Fallback to default language if translation is missing.
- Future: translations may be editable via the admin panel.

👥 User Authorization

- Roles and permissions should be stored in DB.
- Admin panel must be restricted to authorized users only.
- Regenerate session ID after login.
- Optionally, session fingerprinting via browser/IP can be added.

🔁 Backward Compatibility

- Older modules/themes/routes must keep working.
- If needed, use aliasing (core/aliases.php) for legacy support.
- Database changes must not break old functionality.
- All changes logged in process.md.

🗂️ Logging & Versioning

- Every operation must be written to process.md:  
  - Developer  
  - Date  
  - What was done  
  - Why  
  - Affected files  
- GitHub must be used for version control.
- Commits must be short and meaningful.

📌 General Rules

- PHP version: 8.1 or higher.
- Composer or package managers should not be used.
- Tailwind CSS must be used for all UI design.
- System must be extensible, modular, and scalable.
- Each prompt must only add functionality, never break or refactor existing structure.
